  "method": "Five seconds of real CDP wheel events (Input.dispatchMouseEvent, one every 16 ms, not waiting for each acknowledgement; about 300 are sent) on the 200-component canvas at 30% zoom around component 100, with a component selected, while a Chromium trace (Tracing domain: devtools.timeline, frame, cc, viz) records. Frame duration = the time between the presentations of consecutive frames that wanted an update (the compositor PipelineReporter events, inside the window), so it reads 16.7 ms when every vsync made a frame and 33.3 ms after a missed one; missed vsyncs = round(draw-to-draw interval / 16.67) - 1 summed over compositor draws, and dropped/partial frames as the compositor labels them; long tasks = RunTask on CrRendererMain over 16.7 ms. rAF intervals are recorded alongside. \"pan\" is wheel scrolling only; \"panWithZoom\" replaces every twelfth wheel event with a Ctrl-wheel zoom step (one notch, 1.27x; in for a second, out for a second), so the view is zooming throughout. Reported raw and rounded to whole vsyncs: the software compositor stamps presentation times with about +/- 2 ms of jitter around a steady 60 Hz (mean 16.7), so the raw p95 and the count over 17.7 ms measure that jitter as well as real misses. Pass: p95 of the intervals in whole vsyncs <= 16.7 ms, and at most 2% of frames that missed a vsync (interval >= 25 ms) or were dropped, in both runs. Pixels are rasterised on the CPU (--disable-gpu). The benchmark never gives the page a transform."
